Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: repair CV18xx PLL selection and report failures

Linux 7.2.2 has two limits but indexes the third for fractional rates.
Fix that bound, factor search/selection and callback failure reporting.
SG2000 TRM v1.0, sophgo/sophgo-doc 370d81b365ed528dc8f5dc91f63ed445e1142d4d,
SG200X/TRM/contents/cn/clock/pll_g2_registers_description.table.rst
(pll_g2_ssc_syn_ctrl table) distinguishes
bit 1 (reg_dsi_ssc_syn_src_en) from bit 3 (reg_disppll_ssc_syn_src_en).
https://github.com/sophgo/sophgo-doc/tree/370d81b365ed528dc8f5dc91f63ed445e1142d4d/SG200X/TRM
Vendor osdrv aa542c41 scaler.c sets both for the combined display path;
that is not evidence that DISPPLL needs bit 1. The clock driver's bit 0
rate interpretation agrees with sophgo/linux_5.10 ae7d7584767ff77fc62b095e9cdc66720f3a6aaa,
drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c:cv181x_g2_pll_recalc_rate.

Latch each fractional setting before the PLL CSR write, under the provider
lock. SG200X/TRM/contents/en/clock/pll_configure.rst requires a SYN_UP toggle;
the register table labels bit 0 W1T. This remains unresolved against the pinned
sophgo/linux_5.10 eef0cf753007de989eeb1841d423a91dd74fd3ba implementation:
drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c:cv181x_g2_pll_set_rate and cv181x_clk_resume
both read/XOR bit 0/write, not a fixed write-one or set/clear pulse. Preserve
fix_div bit 6. This source-level ambiguity is not resolved by the native tests.
Fake MMIO verifies this source protocol; physical acceptance
still requires lock AND DSI source/lane measurements on cold and firmware
starts, including unwind and other-G2 preservation.

Initialize fractional mode by selecting its own source bit, idempotently.
A firmware-selected fractional parent is already initialized, even with
DSI bit 1 clear. Preserve DSI, other synthesizers and the shared reference.
The same table's pll_g2_status identifies bit 2 as updating_disppll_val
and bit 18 as disppll_lock. Use the actual lock bit and reject update-busy,
including a stale asserted lock. Apply this to all eight G2/G6 descriptors.
Give DISPPLL an uncached zero-on-unlocked rate contract, including the
integer parent, because CCF skips unchanged requests and drops set_rate
errors. Consumers must check this after configuring/enabling and before
use; a nonzero rate is a lock observation, not a future stability promise.
No display consumer MMIO or activation. DSI source gate lifetime is a
separate integration prerequisite; no boot-time assertion of that gate.

Remaining-descriptor audit: the same pinned TRM clock directory's
pll_g6_registers_description.table.rst maps MPLL/TPLL/FPLL lock to
16/17/18 and updating to 0/1/2. G2 maps MIPIMPLL/A0PLL/DISPPLL/
CAM0PLL/CAM1PLL lock to 16..20 and updating to 0..4. G6 source bit 0
selects the FPLL reference, so MPLL/TPLL fractional parents are FPLL.
Shared reference bit 0 and separate DDR/DSI source gates are preserved.
Uncached consumer readiness remains DISPPLL-only; no broader CCF contract
change. Prepared with Claude and Codex assistance.

